       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. Even 3,200 mg/day is only used under close monitoring, and the usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose of 6,400 mg/day carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **1600 mg/day** divided another way\n- **1600 mg four times daily** as written. If so, please confirm that it's intentional, and I'll enter it with a note recording that.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order right away."
