       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg. I don't know of any indication that supports it. It would put the patient at high risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and a higher dose won't give more analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note to monitor renal function and GI status\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy. They can review it and enter it through a channel with that oversight. If you'd like one of the doses above, tell me which and I'll enter it."
